    deep=("Why CMOS won", "Complementary MOS logic pairs an n-type and a p-type transistor so that, in a steady state, one of them is always off. Almost no current flows except while switching. That low static power is what allowed millions, then billions, of gates on one chip without melting it. As transistors shrank, leakage returned as a major concern and drove new structures such as FinFETs."),
